    "habitat": "continental_slope",
    "order": 82,
    "notes": "Long, slender cod-like fish, thicker than an eel, with an ordinary fish head (large mouth, projecting lower jaw, small chin barbel); a short first dorsal and one very long second dorsal and anal fin running to a small rounded tail; blue-grey to bronze-grey above, silvery-grey sides and belly, dark-edged fins. Approximation: no barbel; the two dorsals are one ribbon fin."
